      "findings": [
        "Original shirtless MGS2 filtration-pool Vamp preserved: dark hair/goatee, short horizontal chest scars, natural abdominal wound on anatomicalRIGHT as visible, dark trousers/suspenders/gloves/boots and original-style grooved knives; no MGS4 coat/body/tattoo import.",
        "OriginalPS2 captures16700/16912 physically corroborate face/torso/chestscars/wound; source16920 is Raiden and explicitly excluded.",
        "MainLEFT16 backwards reach remains raw but is not used by throw; newleft-v3 whole forwardLEFT grapple16 routed into active throw, while guard returns preserve base anatomy.",
        "RIGHT19 knife reaches sourcex1399 in1402-wide PNG, native tip appears closed with3pxremaining margin; not clipped at actual alpha16 edge."
      ],
      "limits": [
        "All source PNGs were physically opened, twenty independently authored square-pixel body figures per main direction plus separately whole-body authored LEFT supplements; no bitmap-reduction/filter/mirroring claim.",
        "All figures retain complete natural2arms2legs, full standing boots and naturally compact crouch/KO; per-face noses and forward moves are consistent except explicitly superseded source cells excluded by current routing.",
        "Weak unchanged alpha/RGB fringes remain and are qualified; zero alpha16 outer-edge contacts do not assert every weak fringe absent.",
        "QA V2 is actual decoded-native-source/renderer and modal-geometry evidence; it does NOT contain saved modal/match screenshots and does NOT certify an emitted-engine projectile birth. Independent reviewer did not fabricate such a claim.",
        "Original source display heights/incarnation UID retained; no official1:1 human metric, authentic hardware palette budget or publisher extracted animation certification.",
        "Fine grooved knife geometry is a source-informed pixel approximation; single near/far wound visibility depends on body angle."
      ]
